 <text type="manuscript">
  
  <pb xml:id="leaf001r" facs="duk_nhg.00755_large.jpg" type="recto"/>
  
  <body>
   <p>
    <add place="above">Think a moment what are <add place="below"><metamark target="#a001" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><del rend="overstrike"><add place="above" xml:id="a001"><gap reason="illegible" extent="two words" resp="#ja"/></add></del> the sub <unclear reason="illegible" resp="#ja" cert="low">bases</unclear></add> <add place="below" hand="#h02"><metamark target="#a002 #a003" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" xml:id="a002">to-day</add><add place="above" xml:id="a003">to be</add>
    Books, profoundly considered, show
    a nation more than <del rend="overstrike">their</del> any
    thing else&#8212; more than their laws
    <subst hand="#h02"><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">and</del><add place="above" seq="2">or</add></subst> manners. (This is probably
    the <subst hand="#h02"><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">last</del><add place="above" seq="2">deep-down</add></subst> meaning of th<subst hand="#h02"><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">e</del><add place="above" seq="2">at</add></subst> well-buried but
    ever-vital platitude. Let me make a
    people's song, and I don't care who
    makes their <unclear reason="illegible" resp="#ja" cert="high">laws</unclear>.) Books  
   </p>
   
   <milestone unit="glued"/>
   
   <p>
    <del rend="overstrike">Books</del> <add place="above" hand="#h02">too</add> reflect on <del rend="overstrike">the r</del>
    humanity en-masse, and <del rend="overstrike">give
    the latter a strange glow</del>&#8212;<subst><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">and
    prove</del><add place="above" seq="2">surely show</add></subst> them splendidly <add place="below"><metamark target="#a004" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" xml:id="a004">or the reverse,</add> and prove
    <add place="below" hand="#h02"><metamark target="#a005" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" xml:id="a005" hand="#h02">&amp; celebrate</add>
    their prevalent traits<add place="below" hand="#h02"><metamark target="#a006" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" hand="#h02" xml:id="a006">&#8212;(these last the main things.)</add>
   </p>
   
   <milestone unit="glued"/>
   
   <p>
    Homer has grown out of <add place="below" rend="marked"><metamark target="#a007" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" xml:id="a007">and held the ages, <subst><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">by</del><add place="above" seq="2">and reigns <del rend="overstrike" seq="3">to-day</del><add place="above" seq="4">yet by</add></add></subst></add> the
    prevalent admiration for personal
    prowess and, <del rend="overstrike">and</del> courage, <del rend="overstrike">and</del>
    leadership&#8212;inherent in the
    <add place="above">whole</add>human race. Shakspere
    concentrates the brilliancy
    of <subst><del rend="overstrike" seq="1">the</del><add place="below" rend="marked" seq="2" hand="#h02"><metamark target="#a008" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" xml:id="a008">centuries of</add></subst> fuedalism <add place="below" rend="marked"><metamark target="#a009" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" xml:id="a009">in the personalities produced</add> and <add place="below"><metamark target="#a010" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" xml:id="a010">paints</add> the
    amorous passion. The books
    of the Bible stand for the
    <add place="below"><metamark target="#a011" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" xml:id="a011">final</add>superiority of <del rend="overstrike">the</del> devout <add place="above">emotions and</add>
    intellect over all <add place="below"><metamark target="#a012" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><add place="above" xml:id="a012">the <unclear reason="illegible" resp="#ja" cert="low">rest</unclear></add> and of religious
    adoration<add place="below" hand="#h02">,</add> &amp; <del rend="overstrike" seq="1">of</del><add place="above" seq="2" hand="#h02">of</add> absolute justice,
    <add place="below"><metamark target="#a013" function="add">&#8248;</metamark></add><subst><del rend="overstrike" seq="1"><add place="above" xml:id="a013">finally</add></del><add place="above" seq="2">ultimately</add></subst> more powerful than the haughtiest
    King<add place="inline" hand="#h02">s</add>
   </p>

